      "content": "<!DOCTYPE html>\n<html lang=\"en\">\n<head>\n  <meta charset=\"UTF-8\">\n  <meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0\">\n  <title>Pixel Robot Grid Navigator</title>\n  <link rel=\"stylesheet\" href=\"styles.css\">\n</head>\n<body>\n  <main class=\"card\">\n    <h1>Pixel Robot</h1>\n    <p class=\"subtitle\">Navigate the 5×5 grid</p>\n    <canvas id=\"gridCanvas\" width=\"400\" height=\"400\" aria-label=\"5 by 5 grid with robot\"></canvas>\n    <div class=\"status\" aria-live=\"polite\">\n      <span id=\"positionDisplay\">Position: (0, 0)</span>\n      <span id=\"directionDisplay\">Facing: right</span>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"controls\">\n      <button id=\"forwardBtn\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"Move forward\">Forward</button>\n      <button id=\"turnLeftBtn\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"Turn left\">Turn left</button>\n      <button id=\"turnRightBtn\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"Turn right\">Turn right</button>\n      <button id=\"resetBtn\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"Reset robot\">Reset</button>\n    </div>\n  </main>\n  <script src=\"game.js\"></script>\n</body>\n</html>",
      "description": "Main HTML structure"
    },
    {
      "path": "styles.css",
      "content": ":root {\n  --bg: #1e1e2f;\n  --card-bg: #2a2a40;\n  --primary: #6c63ff;\n  --text: #e0e0e0;\n  --accent: #ffb74d;\n}\n\n* {\n  box-sizing: border-box;\n  margin: 0;\n  padding: 0;\n}\n\nbody {\n  min-height: 100vh;\n  display: flex;\n  align-items: center;\n  justify-content: center;\n  background: var(--bg);\n  font-family: system-ui, -apple-system, 'Segoe UI', Roboto, sans-serif;\n  font-size: 16px;\n  color: var(--text);\n  padding: 1rem;\n}\n\n.card {\n  background: var(--card-bg);\n  border-radius: 1.5rem;\n  padding: 2rem;\n  max-width: 480px;\n  width: 100%;\n  box-shadow: 0 8px 24px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.4);\n  display: flex;\n  flex-direction: column;\n  align-items: center;\n  gap: 1.5rem;\n}\n\nh1 {\n  font-size: 1.75rem;\n  font-weight: 700;\n  color: var(--primary);\n  margin-bottom: -0.5rem;\n}\n\n.subtitle {\n  font-size: 1rem;\n  color: #a0a0b0;\n}\n\ncanvas {\n  width: 100%;\n  max-width: 400px;\n  height: auto;\n  aspect-ratio: 1 / 1;\n  border-radius: 0.75rem;\n  background: #151525;\n  display: block;\n}\n\n.status {\n  display: flex;\n  gap: 1.5rem;\n  flex-wrap: wrap;\n  justify-content: center;\n  font-size: 1.125rem;\n  font-weight: 500;\n}\n\n.controls {\n  display: flex;\n  flex-wrap: wrap;\n  gap: 0.75rem;\n  justify-content: center;\n  width: 100%;\n}\n\nbutton {\n  font-family: inherit;\n  font-size: 1rem;\n  font-weight: 600;\n  padding: 0.75rem 1.25rem;\n  border: none;\n  border-radius: 0.75rem;\n  background: var(--primary);\n  color: #fff;\n  cursor: pointer;\n  transition: background 0.15s, transform 0.1s;\n  min-width: 100px;\n}\n\nbutton:hover {\n  background: #5a52d5;\n}\n\nbutton:focus-visible {\n  outline: 3px solid var(--accent);\n  outline-offset: 2px;\n}\n\nbutton:active {\n  transform: scale(0.96);\n  background: #4a42b5;\n}\n\n#resetBtn {\n  background: var(--accent);\n  color: #1e1e2f;\n}\n\n#resetBtn:hover {\n  background: #ffa726;\n}\n\n#resetBtn:active {\n  background: #f59e0b;\n}\n\n@media (max-width: 400px) {\n  .card {\n    padding: 1.25rem;\n  }\n  button {\n    min-width: 80px;\n    padding: 0.6rem 1rem;\n    font-size: 0.95rem;\n  }\n  .status {\n    font-size: 1rem;\n    gap: 1rem;\n  }\n}\n\n[hidden] {\n  display: none !important;\n}",
      "description": "Styling and responsive layout"
    },
    {
      "path": "game.js",
      "content": "(function () {\n  'use strict';\n\n  const GRID_SIZE = 5;\n  const INITIAL_STATE = { row: 0, col: 0, dir: 'right' };\n\n  const DIRECTIONS = ['up', 'right', 'down', 'left'];\n\n  let state = { ...INITIAL_STATE };\n\n  const canvas = document.getElementById('gridCanvas');\n  const ctx = canvas.getContext('2d');\n  const positionDisplay = document.getElementById('positionDisplay');\n  const directionDisplay = document.getElementById('directionDisplay');\n\n  function turnLeft(dir) {\n    const idx = DIRECTIONS.indexOf(dir);\n    return DIRECTIONS[(idx + 3) % 4];\n  }\n\n  function turnRight(dir) {\n    const idx = DIRECTIONS.indexOf(dir);\n    return DIRECTIONS[(idx + 1) % 4];\n  }\n\n  function moveForward(state) {\n    const { row, col, dir } = state;\n    let newRow = row;\n    let newCol = col;\n    if (dir === 'up') newRow = Math.max(0, row - 1);\n    else if (dir === 'down') newRow = Math.min(GRID_SIZE - 1, row + 1);\n    else if (dir === 'left') newCol = Math.max(0, col - 1);\n    else if (dir === 'right') newCol = Math.min(GRID_SIZE - 1, col + 1);\n    return { row: newRow, col: newCol, dir };\n  }\n\n  function updateDisplay() {\n    positionDisplay.textContent = `Position: (${state.row}, ${state.col})`;\n    directionDisplay.textContent = `Facing: ${state.dir}`;\n  }\n\n  function drawGrid() {\n    const size = canvas.width;\n    const cell = size / GRID_SIZE;\n    ctx.clearRect(0, 0, size, size);\n\n    // Draw grid lines\n    ctx.strokeStyle = '#3a3a5a';\n    ctx.lineWidth = 1;\n    for (let i = 0; i <= GRID_SIZE; i++) {\n      ctx.beginPath();\n      ctx.moveTo(i * cell, 0);\n      ctx.lineTo(i * cell, size);\n      ctx.stroke();\n      ctx.beginPath();\n      ctx.moveTo(0, i * cell);\n      ctx.lineTo(size, i * cell);\n      ctx.stroke();\n    }\n\n    // Draw robot\n    const x = state.col * cell + cell / 2;\n    const y = state.row * cell + cell / 2;\n    const r = cell * 0.3;\n\n    ctx.fillStyle = '#6c63ff';\n    ctx.beginPath();\n    ctx.arc(x, y, r, 0, Math.PI * 2);\n    ctx.fill();\n\n    // Direction indicator (triangle)\n    ctx.fillStyle = '#ffb74d';\n    ctx.beginPath();\n    const angle = { right: 0, down: Math.PI / 2, left: Math.PI, up: -Math.PI / 2 }[state.dir];\n    const tipX = x + Math.cos(angle) * r * 1.6;\n    const tipY = y + Math.sin(angle) * r * 1.6;\n    const leftX = x + Math.cos(angle + Math.PI / 2) * r * 0.6;\n    const leftY = y + Math.sin(angle + Math.PI / 2) * r * 0.6;\n    const rightX = x + Math.cos(angle - Math.PI / 2) * r * 0.6;\n    const rightY = y + Math.sin(angle - Math.PI / 2) * r * 0.6;\n    ctx.moveTo(tipX, tipY);\n    ctx.lineTo(leftX, leftY);\n    ctx.lineTo(rightX, rightY);\n    ctx.closePath();\n    ctx.fill();\n  }\n\n  function render() {\n    updateDisplay();\n    drawGrid();\n  }\n\n  // Button handlers\n  document.getElementById('forwardBtn').addEventListener('click', () => {\n    state = moveForward(state);\n    render();\n  });\n\n  document.getElementById('turnLeftBtn').addEventListener('click', () => {\n    state = { ...state, dir: turnLeft(state.dir) };\n    render();\n  });\n\n  document.getElementById('turnRightBtn').addEventListener('click', () => {\n    state = { ...state, dir: turnRight(state.dir) };\n    render();\n  });\n\n  document.getElementById('resetBtn').addEventListener('click', () => {\n    state = { ...INITIAL_STATE };\n    render();\n  });\n\n  // Initial render\n  render();\n})();",
      "description": "Game logic and canvas rendering"
    },
    {
      "path": "README.md",
      "content": "# Pixel Robot Grid Navigator\n\nAn offline, dependency-free browser app featuring a pixel robot on a 5×5 grid. The robot starts at the top-left corner facing right. Use the buttons to move forward, turn left, turn right, or reset.\n\n## Features\n\n- 5×5 grid with robot position and direction indicator\n- Boundary enforcement: the robot cannot leave the grid\n- Live position and direction display\n- Keyboard-accessible labeled controls with focus, hover, and pressed states\n- Responsive layout down to 360px width\n- Cohesive dark theme with system fonts\n\n## Controls\n\n- **Forward**: Move one cell in the current direction (blocked at grid edges)\n- **Turn left**: Rotate 90° counter-clockwise\n- **Turn right**: Rotate 90° clockwise\n- **Reset**: Return to the starting position (top-left, facing right)\n\n## Usage\n\nOpen `index.html` in any modern browser. No server or network connection required.\n\n## File Structure\n\n- `index.html` — Main HTML structure\n- `styles.css` — Styling and responsive layout\n- `game.js` — Game logic and canvas rendering\n- `README.md` — This file\n\n## Implementation Notes\n\n- Pure HTML, CSS, and plain JavaScript\n- No external assets, imports, or packages\n- Uses `addEventListener` for all event handling\n- Includes `[hidden] { display: none !important; }` CSS rule\n",
      "description": "Documentation"
    }
  ]
}